{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>But I</b> — planted in the house of HaShem. Because Doeg was uprooted, therefore he said: <b>He will uproot you</b>, and your root, from the heavy building. The meaning: to cut off the root, and from the building of the active [participle] to the opposite [i.e., the passive]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:43.432075610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}